INT. CABLE-REPAIR SHIP, FREEZER HOLD - NIGHT

Rime on steel. A string of work lights swinging. Crates stacked to the ceiling, each stamped with a number.

MAEVE KOSTELNY, 30s, parka, ship's cook, drags a crate lid back. Breath fogs.

HARLAN GREER, 50s, bosun, stands in the hatch, one hand on the door.

MAEVE
(to the room)
Anyone down here?

Nothing. A crate shifts, creaks.

HARLAN
Get out of there.

MAEVE
It's counting itself, Harlan.

HARLAN
What?

MAEVE
The crates. There's one more than the manifest. There's always one more.

HARLAN
Maeve.

MAEVE
(muttering)
Thirty-one. Thirty-two. Thirty-three.

HARLAN
(to himself)
Don't look at it. Don't look at it.

MAEVE
I'm not looking.

HARLAN
You're looking.

MAEVE
Then so are you.

HARLAN
I'm looking at you.

MAEVE
Then who's behind me?

Silence. The work lights stop swinging. Both stare at the same spot.

HARLAN
(to everyone, to no one)
All hands up top. All hands up top.

MAEVE
They can't hear you.

HARLAN
(softly)
They never could.

MAEVE
Thirty-four.

The door slams. Locks. Harlan hammers it.

HARLAN
Open it! Open it!

MAEVE
(to herself)
Thirty-five.

She turns, and a crate lid lifts on its own.
